the ledge of the harbor (the grapnel) come up at the bottom. The lower terrace: the orchard, the Gardener and his shed.
The middle terrace: statues and hedges (cover), a crimson lens, Tidekeepers. The upper terrace: the palace, and its gate:
a water lock, in a stone basin that has been dry for a thousand years ("THE GATE OF THE HIGH TIDE RISES ON THE WATER OF
THE TIDE", the tablet by the causeway). A great pipe leaves the basin and runs down the east side of the terraces, over
the edge of the cliff, towards the chimneys of the Foundry: the water came from its great pump. Once the pump runs, the
basin fills, the gate rises, the fountains run.
Two crimson lenses watch the upper terrace: they always see, and their lockdowns bring Tidekeepers.
]]
